            <ArticleTitle>Promising, but still a matter of debate.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>378-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/ccd.26729</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Several trials failed to demonstrate the efficacy of plaque modification device in patients with severely calcified coronary lesions. Safety and efficacy of the Diamondback 360® Coronary OAS have been demonstrated by the ORBIT II trial. The 2-year follow-up of the ORBIT II trial extends the favorable results previously shown at 30-day and 1-year follow-up. The single arm, non-randomized character of the trial with indirect historical comparison may restrict the results to hypothesis generating and entail further prospective randomized trials.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>© 2016 Wiley Periodicals, Inc.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
